redfin 1195: device passcode (SweetKeyStore) + SweetACM (AppleCredentialManager stand-in), kern.sweet_passcode default 0

Prerequisite for Touch ID enrolment: Settings > Touch ID & Passcode > Turn Passcode On, lock/unlock with it.
Design: logs/research/passcode-acm-design-2026-11-18.md.

- bsd/dev/sweet_passcode.c: kern.sweet_passcode (root; 0 = today's behaviour exactly, verifier not read;
  1 passcode + UI lock state; 2 passcode, never reported locked; 3 = 1 locked at boot). Boot-arg
  sweetpasscode=N; sweetpasscode=0 pins it off (sysctl writes refused). kern.sweet_passcode_reset=1 (root)
  stores "no passcode". kern.sweet_passcode_state. Verifier /var/local/keystore/passcode.v1 (root 0600):
  PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256, 100000 iterations, 16-byte random salt; the passcode is never stored or logged.
  Backoff after 5 failures (60 s doubling, cap 15 min), never a wipe. Unreadable file fails open.
- SweetKeyStore (mode != 0 only): sel 7/17/35 live lock state (ss 0x6/0x4/0x5, sls 3/0/1, sfa, sb),
  8/32 lock, 9 unlock_device (copyin, verify, 0xe007c008 wrong), 12 unlock_bag (system bag) verify,
  15 change_secret (old/new pointers in scalars 3..6), 105 epilogue, 40 generation, 42 verify_password
  (packed struct), 3 save_bag ("SWEETKB1"). Wrap/unwrap untouched: the passcode never protects data.
